Use this tool to read/control Nest thermostat state.

`action` (required) — pick exactly ONE per call:
  - `get_status`             → read current state. No other args.
  - `set_target_temperature` → CHANGE THE NUMBER (e.g. "set to 70", "70F", "make it 72"). Requires `target_temperature`.
  - `set_mode`               → CHANGE COOL vs HEAT vs OFF. Requires `mode`.
  - `set_fan_mode`           → CHANGE THE FAN. Requires `fan_mode`.
  - `set_eco_mode`           → ECO ON/OFF. Requires `enabled`.

The action name is `set_target_temperature` (NOT `set_temperature`,
NOT `set_temp`, NOT `change_temperature`). Pass the exact name above.
Aliases are accepted but the canonical name is what you should emit.

Conditional fields (only the one matching your action):
  - `target_temperature` — single Fahrenheit number (e.g. 70). Required for `set_target_temperature`.
  - `mode`               — `HEAT`, `COOL`, `HEATCOOL`, or `OFF`. Required for `set_mode`. Uppercase, no underscores.
  - `fan_mode`           — `ON`, `AUTO`, or `OFF`. Required for `set_fan_mode`.
  - `enabled`            — `true` / `false`. Required for `set_eco_mode`.

Optional:
  - `device_id` — target a specific thermostat (omit for the default).

ONE ACTION PER CALL. If the user wants both a mode change and a target
temperature ("set it to cool at 70"), make TWO sequential calls:
  1. `nest_home_control(action="set_mode", mode="COOL")`
  2. `nest_home_control(action="set_target_temperature", target_temperature=70)`

Don't try to bundle `mode` and `target_temperature` into a single
call — the bridge will run only the action you named and ignore the
extra arg.
